How to attribute
----------------

**Cite the DOI, not this website.** Every gene we have reported carries the DOI
of its report, shown on that gene's page and returned with the record. A DOI
takes your reader to the experiments themselves, and will not move.

A gene with no report published yet has no DOI to cite. Attribute it to Only
Good Antibodies and link its gene page.

If you are redistributing records rather than citing a result, please attribute
the source and keep the gene page link that comes with every record, so a
reader can reach the full result and the report behind it.


Why the data is separate
------------------------

Creative Commons licences are written for content, not software: they do not
address source availability, linking or patents, and Creative Commons
themselves recommend against applying them to code. An open licence on the code
and an open licence on the data are two different grants, so they are stated in
two files rather than blurred into one.
